The paper title, author order, arXiv identifier, and arXiv-issued DOI were
checked against the public arXiv record on 2026-11-10. Version 1 was submitted
on 2026-10-19. An arXiv preprint is not a claim of journal acceptance.

This archive contains five Lean 4 source packages for binary finite-assignment
models and related graph formulas. See THEOREM_MAP.txt for exact public theorem
names, assumptions, and limits of the claims. The release documentation and
portable dependency metadata were revised without changing the Lean sources.

Contents
  Core2      Two-block assignment and signed-sum formulas.
  Core3      The Core3tree package; generalized three-block tree formulas.
  TreeGraph  Weighted rooted-tree model formulas and raw-source interfaces.
  Core3loop  Three-block triangle signed-sum formula, including parity cases.
  Core4loop  Square, triangle plus leaf, diamond, and complete graph K4.

Each directory has its own README, lean-toolchain, lakefile.toml, and
lake-manifest.json. Core3 is the archive directory name; its Lean package and
import root are Core3tree, and its principal theorem namespace is No13Migration.
TreeGraph includes its required Core2 and Core3tree sources locally. Core4loop
requires the sibling Core3loop directory; preserve the relative folder layout.

Publish all five folders together, with this README at the repository root.
There is no root Lake package. See GITHUB_UPLOAD.txt for the upload checklist,
commit-identity privacy, and release/version guidance. Git-based upload is
recommended; do not upload only the ZIP in place of the extracted sources.

Start with BUILDING.txt for prerequisites, pinned dependency setup, and build
commands. No compilation was performed for this packaging revision. The static
checks and their limits are recorded in VERIFICATION.txt. SHA256SUMS records
the packaged file contents; verification commands are in BUILDING.txt.

The Core4 endpoints evaluate raw finite-assignment signed sums over F2. Their
corrected exponents must be distinguished from the retained historical ones.
This archive does not certify the manuscript's contraction-to-assignment bridge
or its Core4 proper-support/Gamma extraction as part of those endpoints.
TreeGraph's general raw-assignment statements have explicit certificate
hypotheses; they must not be presented as unconditional arbitrary-tree results.

The archive excludes dependency checkouts, compiled Lake artifacts, temporary
probes, and work reports. Source counts include blank and comment lines and may
include shared code in more than one package.

The source release uses the MIT License in LICENSE; see REUSE_NOTICE.txt for
reuse details. SOURCE_PROVENANCE.txt records the source binding. CITATION.txt
and ARXIV_NOTES.txt describe citation and arXiv submission considerations.
The root CITATION file identifies the paper; CITATION.txt includes its ORCIDs
and citation guidance. CITATION.bib supplies an arXiv-preprint BibTeX
entry. Paper authorship does not change the MIT notice or assign Git commit
authorship. Cite an exact repository commit for source reproducibility.
